MQTT candidate automated board acceptance, 2026-11-05

Purpose
- complete the board path without an external RS485 slave or a human touch
- keep every shortcut in a diagnostic-only Kconfig image
- preserve the production path: real Modbus samples and local touch remain
  required when CONFIG_VG_CONFIG_ACCEPTANCE_FIXTURE is disabled

Diagnostic image
- command: bash scripts/build.sh --config-fixture
- temporary local TLS CA and synthetic device credentials were used
- CONFIG_VG_CONFIG_ACCEPTANCE_FIXTURE=y
- CONFIG_VG_OTA_TEST_FIXTURES=y
- A/B image size: 1689856 bytes
- check_fw_images: OK A=0x90000000 B=0x90800000
- SRAM static use: 388624/524288 bytes (74.12%)

Fixture behavior
- normal acquisition still runs through vg_ui_backend_apply_live and
  vg_model_set_live
- deterministic raw values keep every configured point online and outside
  alarm thresholds
- the production confirmation surface is rendered first
- only after the surface has remained visible for 3000 ms does the fixture
  invoke the same local confirmation event used by the touch button
- no MQTT or Agent request can invoke this action

End-to-end result
- TLS Broker authenticated the device and accepted its config subscription
- foreign device, retained and wrong-direction messages were rejected
- query returned the current table
- open returned a session and lease
- put reached awaiting_local_confirm
- an exact duplicate put preserved state_seq and confirmation_id
- the local UI action sent the frozen confirmation binding
- result state: applied
- committed table grew from 15 to 16 points
- new point s9_f3_r0 was present in points.json
- vgpoint get reported all 16 points online under the fixture
- pending_alarm.txt was absent after the startup stale-file fix
- SWD reset without reflashing retained all 16 points and resumed local
  acquisition while the TLS Broker was offline

Acceptance command result
PASS config MQTT board apply: mode=local-tls
device=vg-09001a800451383430303835 points=16
query=ok open=ok put=awaiting_local_confirm
local_confirm=applied persisted=ok

Production gate
- scripts/ota/check_release.py rejects images with
  CONFIG_VG_CONFIG_ACCEPTANCE_FIXTURE enabled
- release check also reports test fixtures and the local test CA
- the final production build disables both fixture symbols and passes the
  regular release check
- production A/B size: 1681912 bytes
- production SHA-256:
  A=3cc6a70bd6f6ed111e275a0e04f824170c33b587bf2bcd2cd8e9a64b12abc761
  B=89da43e65e874f0d8dd54e84e73d2a806a1f76d1df15d4eab15159b3a77ccce6
- production smoke after flashing:
  n=14 canonical scene table restored
  CONFIG_VG_CONFIG_ACCEPTANCE_FIXTURE is not set
  CONFIG_VG_OTA_TEST_FIXTURES is not set
  vgconfig-mqtt initialized=0 error=trust_unconfigured
  local firmware booted normally with no test CA
- synthetic MQTT credentials were wiped after acceptance:
  vgconfigmqtt: wiped
  ls /data/velaguard/provision/config_mqtt_secrets.v1 -> stat failed: 2

Scope note
- this is automated acceptance through the real HMI confirmation path, not a
  claim that a person touched the screen
- production firmware keeps the touch-only confirmation requirement
- an external physical sensor and a wall-power interruption are separate
  hardware procedures, not prerequisites for the software acceptance fixture
